<h2>🐘 PHP pools <small style="color:var(--muted)">one FPM master per account — shell functions off, jailed, CPU/RAM capped</small></h2>
<div class="card"><form class="inline" method="post" action="/admin/php-pools-apply" onsubmit="return confirm('Regenerate pool(s) from the hardened template? Active PHP processes reload.')"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<?=Helpers::csrf()?>"><input type="hidden" name="target" value="--all"><button class="btn">🛡️ Harden all pools</button></form>
<small style="color:var(--muted)">Hardened = <code>disable_functions</code> blocks <code>exec,system,…</code>, <code>open_basedir</code> jails to the home dir, 256M per script, niced below system services. <code>mail()</code>, curl and file access are untouched — WordPress keeps working. Re-applied automatically for new pools and weekly by cron.<br>
Own master = the account's PHP runs in its own process group with RAM, CPU and process caps. RAM and process caps scale with the worker count; the CPU cap is the same for every account (half the cores, at least one): a runaway site slows or restarts its own PHP only, never the database or mail. Each account also gets its own <code>/dev/shm</code>. A master starts on the first request (about 0.1&nbsp;s) and stops after 10 minutes without one, so an idle account has no PHP processes running.</small></div>
<div class="card"><form method="get" action="/admin/php-pools" style="display:flex;gap:6px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:6px"><input type="search" name="q" value="<?=Helpers::e($q ?? '')?>" placeholder="🔍 search username" style="max-width:260px;margin:0"><?php if(($q ?? '')!==''):?><a class="btn small ghost" href="/admin/php-pools">Clear</a><?php endif;?></form>
<?php if(empty($err) && ($sum['all'] ?? 0) > 0):?><p class="muted" style="margin:6px 0"><?=(int)$sum['all']?> pool<?=$sum['all'] == 1 ? '' : 's'?> · <?=(int)$sum['active']?> running now · <?php if($sum['problem']):?><span class="pill err"><?=(int)$sum['problem']?> need attention</span> (listed first)<?php else:?>all hardened, own master<?php endif;?></p><?php endif;?>
<table><tr><th>User</th><th>PHP</th><th>Workers</th><th>Memory</th><th>Nice</th><th>Hardened</th><th>Master</th><th>RAM used / cap</th><th>CPU cap</th><th></th></tr>
<?php foreach($pools ?? [] as $p):?><tr><td><?=Helpers::e($p['user'])?></td><td><span class="pill"><?=Helpers::e($p['ver'])?></span></td><td><?=Helpers::e($p['children'])?></td><td><?=Helpers::e($p['memory'])?></td><td><?=Helpers::e($p['nice'])?></td>
<td><?php if(($p['hardened'] ?? 'no') === 'yes'):?><span class="pill">yes</span><?php else:?><span class="pill err">no</span><?php endif;?></td>
<td><?php if($p['master'] !== 'own'):?><span class="pill warn">shared</span><?php elseif($p['state'] === 'active'):?><span class="pill">own</span><?php elseif($p['state'] === 'idle'):?><span class="pill" title="stopped until the next request">own · idle</span><?php else:?><span class="pill err">own · <?=Helpers::e($p['state'])?></span><?php endif;?></td>
<td><?=$p['master'] === 'own' ? Helpers::e($p['ram']).' / '.Helpers::e($p['ramcap']).' MB' : '—'?></td><td><?=$p['master'] === 'own' ? Helpers::e($p['cpucap']).'%' : '—'?></td>
<td><form method="post" action="/admin/php-pools-apply" style="display:inline"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<?=Helpers::csrf()?>"><input type="hidden" name="target" value="<?=Helpers::e($p['user'])?>"><button class="btn small">Harden</button></form></td></tr><?php endforeach;?>
<?php if(!empty($err)):?><tr><td colspan="10"><span class="pill warn">not loaded</span> <?=Helpers::e($err)?></td></tr><?php elseif(empty($pools ?? []) && ($q ?? '') !== ''):?><tr><td colspan="10" style="color:var(--muted)">No pool matches “<?=Helpers::e($q)?>”.</td></tr><?php elseif(empty($pools ?? [])):?><tr><td colspan="10" style="color:var(--muted)">No user pools yet — created automatically with the first domain.</td></tr><?php endif;?></table>
<?php $pagerBase = '/admin/php-pools?'.(($q ?? '') !== '' ? 'q='.urlencode($q).'&' : ''); $pagerLabel = 'pools'; require __DIR__.'/_pager.php'; ?></div>
